content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-109 - AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-23500",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 85 C. The HF-300 limits are normal up to 70 C, alarm at 80 C and trip at 90 C. The reading is 5 C above the alarm limit and 5 C below the trip limit, so it is in the alarm band and the pump does not need to stop now.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The temperature limits apply to the housing surface, which is where bearing temperatures are measured on the HF-300. A handheld IR reading taken on the housing surface is therefore comparable with these limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration is 2.5 mm/s. On HF-300 Figure 3 this falls in Zone A (0.0 to 2.8 mm/s RMS, 'New machines'), below the 2.8 mm/s Zone A/B boundary. No vibration action is needed. This assumes the reading is RMS velocity and is the highest of the two bearing housings, as the classification method requires.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so the 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom does not apply. The only active symptom is high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing of the drive-end bearing. This is the first listed cause of high bearing temperature, and it fits best because there is no noise and vibration is low (Zone A).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear. This is a listed cause of high bearing temperature, but the absence of noise and the low vibration make it less likely.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment. This is a listed cause of high bearing temperature, but it is less likely given the low vibration (misalignment is also a listed high-vibration cause).",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Confirm the reading. Re-measure the drive-end and non-drive-end bearing housing surface temperatures, and vibration velocity on both housings. Classify the highest vibration reading against Figure 3. Monitor the temperature against the 80 C alarm and 90 C trip limits until the work is complete.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the drive-end bearing, since over-greasing is the first listed cause of high bearing temperature. Correct any over-greasing, then re-check the temperature trend.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool. Tolerances are 0.05 mm parallel offset and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Only if the bearings are found worn, or the temperature stays high after the grease and alignment checks: replace both bearings as a pair (drive-end 6312-C3 and non-drive-end 6310-C3). Do not replace the drive-end bearing alone.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, tighten the bearing housing bolts (M12) to 85 Nm with lightly oiled threads. If the casing is opened, tighten the casing bolts (M16) to 210 Nm and the impeller nut (M24) to 160 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, re-align with the laser tool to 0.05 mm parallel and 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular. Then restart and verify that the bearing temperature returns to 70 C or below and vibration stays in Zone A.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the mechanical seal is disturbed during this work, this serial (HF3-23500) must use cartridge seal HF3-450B with the seal gland nuts at 30 Nm, not 25 Nm. Replace shaft sleeve HF3-455 if scoring is deeper than 0.1 mm, and fit a new casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3. Only needed if bearing replacement is required; it is replaced as a pair with HF3-510.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3. Only needed if bearing replacement is required; it is replaced as a pair with HF3-512.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate (and drain if the casing or seal is opened) the pump before any intrusive work.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required if it is removed.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Trip limit is 90 C. If the drive-end housing temperature reaches 90 C before the work is done, stop the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal flush is Plan 11 from the pump discharge. Never run the pump dry during checks or restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair), if required: 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal and seal gland torque. Manual Table 5 and the parts list give component seal HF3-450 with gland nuts at 25 Nm. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) applies to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. It supersedes HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B and raises the gland torque to 30 Nm. P-109 is serial HF3-23500, which is at or above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies: use HF3-450B and 30 Nm if the seal is disturbed. All other Table 5 torques are unchanged.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C11",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "The documents give no correct grease quantity, grease type or relubrication interval for the HF-300 bearings, so the technician cannot verify 'over-greasing' against a specified value.",
    "No detailed bearing replacement procedure is provided. It is not stated whether bearing replacement requires removing the back pull-out assembly or disturbing the mechanical seal, so it is unknown whether seal HF3-450B, sleeve HF3-455 or gasket HF3-120 will be needed.",
    "It is not confirmed whether the 2.5 mm/s reading is RMS velocity or whether it is the highest of the two bearing housings.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing temperature, the temperature trend history and any recent lubrication or maintenance history are not reported.",
    "The IR gun's emissivity setting and accuracy on the housing surface are unknown, so the 85 C reading should be confirmed.",
    "No labour time is given for a grease quantity check."
  ]
}
